<Base title="The Opening — Development case study" paper>
<main id="main" class="case-page"><a class="back-link" href="/#work"><svg class="icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 8H2M7 3 2 8l5 5"/></svg> All work</a><div class="case-intro"><p class="eyebrow">SELF-INITIATED / DEVELOPMENT PLACEHOLDER / 2026</p><h1 id="route-heading" tabindex="-1">A frame.<br/>With a point<br/><em>of view.</em></h1><div><p class="case-lead">The Opening</p><p>Three rigid leaves. One visible idea. A visitor-directed study in how an interface can feel alive without getting in the way.</p><p class="placeholder-label">Not approved portfolio evidence.</p></div></div>
<div class="case-image"><img src="/art/study.svg" alt="Original three-leaf form study showing independent pivots and a protected central opening" width="960" height="640" fetchpriority="high"/></div>
<div class="case-facts"><div><h2>Contribution</h2><p>Code, graybox geometry and diagrams authored in this Codex session with AI assistance. Personal authorship and role require owner review.</p></div><div><h2>Project status</h2><p>Working Scenes 1–3 slice. Not a client commission. No business outcomes, live deliverable or performance certification claimed.</p></div><div><h2>Collaborators & provenance</h2><p>No external collaborators supplied. Original procedural geometry and SVG; no stock imagery. System fonts. Third-party packages recorded in the lockfile.</p></div></div>
<section class="decision"><span>01 / ART DIRECTION</span><div><h2>Negative space<br/>does the revealing.</h2><p>Unequal chamfered leaves create an open architectural corner. The image is ordinary HTML, already present in the opening. A coral printed seam marks the cut; there is no shutter, circular iris or hidden content.</p><a href="/art/manifest.json">Inspect geometry & pivot manifest <svg class="icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10"/></svg></a></div></section>
<section class="decision"><span>02 / MOTION</span><div><h2>Direction, immediately.<br/>Motion, in response.</h2><p>Precise, Playful and Cinematic commit selection immediately. Three sibling pivots overlap in a weighted score. New input retargets from the rendered pose; repeating the current direction does not replay it. Scrolling away settles the chosen posture.</p><a href="/">Try the working study <svg class="icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10"/></svg></a></div></section>
<section class="decision"><span>03 / ENGINEERING</span><div><h2>The experience<br/>survives the scene.</h2><p>Static HTML carries the meaning and links. One lazy Three.js renderer owns the decorative stage. Light, reduced motion and rendering failure retain authored stills. Native page navigation remains authoritative; supported browsers match the same project image into this case study.</p></div></section>
<section class="case-limitations"><h2>What remains to be proven</h2><p>Owner-approved identity and exact project contribution credits, a real contact destination, physical-device performance and cross-browser motion review. Repository-selected projects are now presented separately. This page exposes development decisions; it does not stand in for a delivered client project.</p><a class="button primary" href="/start/">Keep the direction <span><svg class="icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10"/></svg></span></a></section>
</main></Base>
